ctions at SIGTERM while still letting in-flight ops complete, so a landing burst cannot re-pin the retiring port for the full grace window.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Current docstring: 'Stopping intake first is what keeps a newly-arriving op from extending the drain window indefinitely.' (_mcp_health.py:686-688)","Plan: 'set server.should_exit=True only AFTER the gauge hits 0'","Plan invariant: '>0 in-flight => full grace_seconds drain'","RCA mechanism 1: a retiring container pins a port ~20 min -> next mcp deploy hits port-exhausted"],"finding":"Fix 1 reorders make_sigterm_handler to defer server.should_exit until the gauge drains to 0, but does not address that this re-opens the NEW-connection intake window that the current handler deliberately closes first ('Stopping intake first is what keeps a newly-arriving op from extending the drain window indefinitely', _mcp_health.py:684-689). With intake still open during drain, a burst of new certified ops can hold the gauge >0 and pin the retiring container for the full grace_seconds — re-creating the ~20-min port pin that is the very port-exhaustion mechanism Fix 1 targets.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcf309d4b93fdd9c8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach -> Fix 1 (reorder _on_sigterm to drain first); _mcp_health.py:692-699","norm_id":"n6baa7ac4740b26d9","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A landing burst arrives during a container's drain window; new certified ops keep the gauge >0, so the retiring container stays should_exit=False and pins its port for up to 1200s despite being scheduled for retirement."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have SIGTERM stop accepting NEW connections immediately (uvicorn's lifespan/socket close) while the in-flight gauge still governs when the process actually exits — i.e. keep intake-stop-first but gate the final 